## 🚀 Production Use Case: The Global Financial Performance Matrix## The Business Scenario
You need to extract a dataset from a Finance cube. Your requirements are granular:

   1. Columns: You only want the Amount measure, but paired only with accounts that have the dynamic text attribute "Reporting_Group" = "Operating Expenses".
   2. Rows: You want to stitch a specific pre-defined TM1 subset for Regions ("European_Hubs") against only leaf-level zero elements (n-elements) of your Product dimension to prevent double-counting consolidations.
   3. Context Filter: You want to slice the data specifically targeting the Actual version, the 2026 year, and the Jan month hierarchy elements.

## Complete Blueprint Execution Script

from TM1py.Services import TM1Servicefrom advanced_mdx_engine import AdvancedMdxEngine
# 1. Define configurations using explicit MDX/TM1 conceptscolumn_definition = [
    {
        "dimension": "Account",
        "hierarchy": "Default",
        # Filters elements where attribute matches text criteria
        "attribute_filter": {"Reporting_Group": "Operating Expenses"} 
    },
    {
        "dimension": "Measures",
        "hierarchy": "Default",
        # Isolate exact explicit unique members
        "specific_members": ["Amount"] 
    }
]
row_definition = [
    {
        "dimension": "Region",
        "hierarchy": "Default",
        # Pull from an existing TM1 subset
        "subset": "European_Hubs" 
    },
    {
        "dimension": "Product",
        "hierarchy": "ByCategory",
        # Isolate level 0 elements (Leaf/Data nodes only)
        "level": 0 
    }
]
# 2. Build the query using the Advanced Enginemdx_statement = (
    AdvancedMdxEngine(cube_name="Finance")
    .configure_columns(column_definition)
    .configure_rows(row_definition, suppress_zeros=True)
    # Define exact coordinate context tuple (Dimension, Hierarchy, Element)
    .configure_context_filter([
        ("Version", "Default", "Actual"),
        ("Year", "Default", "2026"),
        ("Month", "Default", "Jan")
    ])
    .generate()
)

print("Generated Advanced MDX:\n", mdx_statement)
# 3. Pipeline extraction to Pandaswith TM1Service(address="localhost", port=8001, user="admin", password="apple", ssl=True) as tm1:
    df = tm1.cubes.cells.execute_mdx_dataframe(mdx_statement)
    print("\nResulting Clean DataFrame Snapshot:\n", df)

